I can think of three ways that might be applicable in different
situations.  Not all of them are equally good:

   a) Play a wizard, where your first items are already identified.
   b) Leave them lying around, and see if the monsters use them
      Certainly not My chosen alternative, but it Does lie within
      the scope of the question.
   c) Use a scroll or spellbook of identify.  Of course, this means
      determining which scroll is a scroll of identify (which is
      usually done by random methods).

You can minimize your random experimentation if you collect a pile of
scrolls.  Scrolls of identify tend to be among the more common ones.
Other common scrolls are usually safe to determine by random means.

But like was mentioned before, try to avoid reading random cursed scrolls,
especially if you don't know whether a scroll is cursed or not.
I admit that I will read cursed or presumedly-cursed scrolls, but
I factor that into my preparations for the experiment.

